course: dictionary
lesson: 2323
title: Counting beats with the crotchet
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A crotchet is a musical note that lasts for one beat in most music. Think of a beat as one tap of your foot. «In 4/4 time each bar holds four crotchet beats.» So you tap four times in each bar, and each tap is one crotchet.
explain: Notes can last longer or shorter. A minim lasts two beats, so it fills two crotchet taps. A quaver lasts half a beat, so two quavers fit into one crotchet. It works like fractions in maths: one whole, two halves, four quarters.
explain: A rest is a counted silence. «A rest is a counted silence and is part of the bar.» When you see a rest, you still count the beat without playing anything.
fact: A crotchet is a note that lasts one beat in most music.
fact: In the USA a crotchet is called a quarter note.
fact: «In 3/4 time each bar holds three crotchet beats, the swaying feel of a waltz.»
fact: «A minim and two crotchets fill a bar exactly» in 4/4 time, because two plus two makes four beats.
fact: Crotchet also has an old-fashioned meaning: a strange, fixed idea or habit.
exercise: «In 4/4 time each bar holds four crotchet beats.» How many crotchet beats are in one bar of 4/4 time? | *Four | Eight | Three | Two
exercise: «A minim lasts two beats.» How many crotchets fill the same time as one minim? | *Two | One | Four | Half
exercise: A crotchet in Britain is called what in the USA? | Eighth note | Half note | *Quarter note | Whole note
test: «3/4 means three crotchet beats in each bar, which gives the swaying feel of a waltz.» What kind of dance does this swaying feel suggest? | *A waltz | A fast race | A football chant | A drum roll
test: A quaver lasts how many beats? | One beat | *Half a beat | Four beats | Two beats
exam: In 4/4 time, a minim is followed by which notes to fill the bar exactly? | Three crotchets | Four minims | *Two crotchets | One quaver
